   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Sand is added to and removed from a pile. Let A(t) be the amount of sand in the pile, in tons, at time t hours, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). The rate of change of A is \\( R(t) = 8 - 6 t \\) tons per hour. At time t = 1, there are 50 tons. Find the value of \\( A(4) \\), in tons, and show the setup for the calculation.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 29,
      "units": "tons"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The known value and the accumulated change combine as \\( A(4) = A(1) + \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(8 - 6 t\\right)\\,dt \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99033",
         "rule_named": "net change theorem"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "An antiderivative of the rate is \\( - 3 t^{2} + 8 t \\), so the integral is \\( \\left[- 3 t^{2} + 8 t\\right]_{1}^{4} = -21 \\).",
         "mathjson": -21,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99003",
         "rule_named": "Fundamental Theorem of Calculus"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "So \\( A(4) = 50 + \\left(-21\\right) = 29 \\) tons.",
         "mathjson": 29,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "combine with the known value"
      }
   ],
